The class `LetterTools` contains static methods that analyze strings of lowercase letters.

```java
public class LetterTools {
    /** Returns the number of indexes i where the character at i equals the character at i + 1. */
    public static int countDoubles(String s) { /* to be implemented in part (a) */ }
    /** Returns the length of the longest run of identical adjacent characters. */
    public static int longestRun(String s) { /* to be implemented in part (b) */ }
}
```

Examples: `countDoubles("zyzxyx")` returns 0 and `longestRun("zyzxyx")` returns 1; `countDoubles("zyxxxzzz")` returns 4 and `longestRun("zyxxxzzz")` returns 3; `countDoubles("xzyyxxz")` returns 2 and `longestRun("xzyyxxz")` returns 2.

A `ScoreKeeper` records the scores of one player. The class also tracks the total number of scores recorded by all ScoreKeeper objects.


• `ScoreKeeper(String name)` creates a keeper with no scores.

• `void addScore(int s)` records a score.

• `double getAverage()` returns the average score, or 0.0 if there are none.

• `int getBest()` returns the highest score, or -1 if there are none.

• `static int getTotalScores()` returns the number of scores recorded by all keepers.

Example:

```java
ScoreKeeper a = new ScoreKeeper("Ana");
ScoreKeeper b = new ScoreKeeper("Gus");
a.addScore(64);
a.addScore(67);
a.addScore(99);
b.addScore(53);
b.addScore(90);
a.getAverage();               // returns 76.667
a.getBest();                  // returns 99
ScoreKeeper.getTotalScores(); // returns 5
```

